      "Title": "Exam GMAT Test topic 1 question 1 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Roy is now 4 years older than Erik and half of that amount older than Iris. If in 2 years, Roy will be twice as old as Erik, then in 2 years what would be Roy's age multiplied by Iris's age?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. 28"
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. 48"
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. 50"
            }
          ]
        },
        "E": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "E. 52"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: C \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Translate piece by piece into numbers. R (Roy) = E (Erik) + 4. The second equation: R = I (Iris) + 2."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The third equation: R +7 = 2(E + 7). We have three equations with three variables."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Roy is 6, Iris is 4 and Erik is 2. In four years Erik would be 6 and Iris 8, the answer is 48."
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
